---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import {
  APP_VERSION,
  INSTALLER,
  INSTALLER_SIZE,
  INSTALLER_SIGNED,
  RELEASES_URL,
  REPO_URL,
} from '../lib/site';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const installerHref = `${base}/downloads/${INSTALLER.file}`;

// The click-through path, written as literal UI strings so a user can match
// them against what's on their screen. Keep these exact - paraphrasing the
// button labels is what makes "just click More info" advice useless.
const steps = [
  {
    n: '01',
    title: 'A blue window appears',
    body: 'It says "Windows protected your PC" and offers a single "Don\'t run" button. It looks like a dead end. It isn\'t: the escape hatch is deliberately understated.',
  },
  {
    n: '02',
    title: 'Click "More info"',
    body: 'It\'s the small grey link in the body text, above the button. This is the step almost everyone misses.',
  },
  {
    n: '03',
    title: 'Click "Run anyway"',
    body: 'A second button appears once the details expand. Before you click it, check the publisher line matches what this page says below.',
  },
];
---

<Layout
  title="Limnia · Install & verify"
  description="Why Windows flags the Limnia installer, how to check it's really ours with a SHA-256 hash, and how to install it safely."
  path="/install"
>
  <main class="relative z-10">
    <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 pt-20 pb-24 sm:px-10 sm:pt-28">
      <header class="mb-14 grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 md:grid-cols-12">
        <div
          class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-ink-faint md:col-span-3"
        >
          / install
        </div>
        <div class="md:col-span-9">
          <h1
            class="font-display text-[40px] font-semibold leading-[1.03] tracking-[-0.03em] text-ink sm:text-[56px]"
          >
            Windows will<br />warn you.
          </h1>
          <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-[17px] leading-[1.6] text-ink-muted">
            That warning is real, and we&rsquo;d rather explain it than hope you
            click through. Here&rsquo;s exactly what it means, why it happens,
            and how to prove this file is the one we built.
          </p>
        </div>
      </header>

      <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-14">
        {/* ── The honest explanation ─────────────────────────────── */}
        <section>
          <h2
            class="font-display text-[24px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink"
          >
            What the warning actually means
          </h2>
          <div class="mt-4 space-y-4 text-[16.5px] leading-[1.65] text-ink-muted">
            <p>
              Windows SmartScreen doesn&rsquo;t scan Limnia and decide
              it&rsquo;s malicious. It checks whether it has seen this exact
              file before, from a publisher it recognises. Limnia is new and
              {INSTALLER_SIGNED ? ' recently signed' : ' not code-signed yet'},
              so the answer is no. And &ldquo;unrecognised&rdquo; is displayed
              with the same red urgency as &ldquo;dangerous.&rdquo;
            </p>
            <p>
              A code-signing certificate costs roughly $110 to $180 a year,
              and since Microsoft&rsquo;s 2026 policy change it no longer buys
              instant trust: even a signed installer keeps warning until
              enough people have downloaded it. So the certificate would soften
              the wording, not remove the wall. We&rsquo;d rather be straight
              with you about that than quietly pass the cost on.
            </p>
            <p class="text-ink">
              The permanent fix is the Microsoft Store, where Microsoft signs
              the package themselves and SmartScreen never fires. That work is
              underway.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        {/* ── Click-through steps ────────────────────────────────── */}
        <section>
          <h2
            class="font-display text-[24px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink"
          >
            Getting past it
          </h2>
          <ol class="mt-6 space-y-0">
            {steps.map((s) => (
              <li
                class="grid grid-cols-[3rem_1fr] gap-x-4 border-t border-line py-5 last:border-b"
              >
                <span
                  class="font-mono text-[12px] uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-pen"
                  >{s.n}</span
                >
                <div>
                  <p class="text-[16px] font-medium text-ink">{s.title}</p>
                  <p class="mt-1.5 text-[15.5px] leading-[1.6] text-ink-muted">
                    {s.body}
                  </p>
                </div>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ol>
        </section>

        {/* ── Verification - the part that earns the trust ────────── */}
        <section>
          <h2
            class="font-display text-[24px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink"
          >
            Don&rsquo;t take our word for it
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-4 text-[16.5px] leading-[1.65] text-ink-muted">
            &ldquo;Trust me&rdquo; is not a security model. Check the file
            against the hash below. If it matches, the installer you have
            is byte-for-byte the one we published. If it doesn&rsquo;t,
            don&rsquo;t run it, and
            <a
              href={`${REPO_URL}/issues`}
              class="text-ink underline decoration-line-strong underline-offset-[3px] transition-colors hover:text-pen hover:decoration-pen"
              >tell us</a
            >.
          </p>

          <div class="mt-6 overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-line bg-surface-raised">
            <dl
              class="grid grid-cols-[7rem_1fr] gap-x-4 gap-y-2.5 px-5 py-4 font-mono text-[12.5px]"
            >
              <dt class="uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-ink-faint">file</dt>
              <dd class="text-ink">{INSTALLER.file}</dd>
              <dt class="uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-ink-faint">version</dt>
              <dd class="text-ink">{APP_VERSION}</dd>
              <dt class="uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-ink-faint">size</dt>
              <dd class="text-ink">
                {INSTALLER_SIZE} ({INSTALLER.bytes.toLocaleString('en-US')} bytes)
              </dd>
              <dt class="uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-ink-faint">sha-256</dt>
              <dd class="break-all text-pen">{INSTALLER.sha256}</dd>
            </dl>
          </div>

          <p
            class="mt-6 font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-ink-faint"
          >
            verify in powershell
          </p>
          <pre
            class="mt-2 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-line bg-surface-sunken px-5 py-4 font-mono text-[13px] leading-[1.7] text-ink-muted"><code>Get-FileHash .\{INSTALLER.file} -Algorithm SHA256 | Format-List</code></pre>
          <p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-[1.6] text-ink-muted">
            Compare the <span class="font-mono text-ink">Hash</span> line to the
            SHA-256 above. Case doesn&rsquo;t matter. You can also upload the
            file to
            <a
              href="https://www.virustotal.com/gui/home/upload"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              target="_blank"
              class="text-ink underline decoration-line-strong underline-offset-[3px] transition-colors hover:text-pen hover:decoration-pen"
              >VirusTotal</a
            > for an independent multi-engine scan.
          </p>
        </section>

        {/* ── What it does on your machine ───────────────────────── */}
        <section>
          <h2
            class="font-display text-[24px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink"
          >
            What the installer touches
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-4 text-[16.5px] leading-[1.65] text-ink-muted">
            The whole footprint, so nothing is a surprise:
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2.5 text-[15.5px] leading-[1.6] text-ink-muted">
            {[
              ['Program Files\\Limnia', 'limnia.exe is 1.2 MB, with no bundled runtime and no services. Next to it the installer drops its own 4 MB uninstaller, which is bigger than Limnia itself. That is Inno Setup, not us. Both go on uninstall.'],
              ['%APPDATA%\\Limnia\\config.json', 'Your last-used tool, color, and brush size. Deleted on uninstall.'],
              ['Start menu + optional desktop shortcut', 'The desktop one is a checkbox you can decline.'],
              ['Optional "start with Windows" entry', 'One HKCU Run registry value, also a checkbox, also removed on uninstall.'],
            ].map(([what, why]) => (
              <li class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-x-4 sm:grid-cols-[20rem_1fr]">
                <span class="font-mono text-[13px] text-ink">{what}</span>
                <span>{why}</span>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-5 text-[16.5px] leading-[1.65] text-ink-muted">
            No network requests, no telemetry, no auto-updater phoning home. The
            <a
              href={`${base}/privacy`}
              class="text-ink underline decoration-line-strong underline-offset-[3px] transition-colors hover:text-pen hover:decoration-pen"
              >privacy page</a
            > covers this in full.
          </p>
        </section>

        {/* ── Download ───────────────────────────────────────────── */}
        <section class="border-t border-line pt-10">
          <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
            <a
              href={installerHref}
              class="group inline-flex items-center gap-2.5 rounded-md bg-ink px-5 py-3 text-[14px] font-semibold text-surface transition-colors hover:bg-pen"
            >
              Download {APP_VERSION}
              <span
                class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium opacity-60 transition-transform group-hover:translate-y-0.5"
                >&darr; {INSTALLER_SIZE}</span
              >
            </a>
            <a
              href={RELEASES_URL}
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              target="_blank"
              class="inline-flex items-center gap-2.5 rounded-md border border-line px-5 py-3 text-[14px] font-medium text-ink transition-colors hover:border-line-strong hover:bg-surface-raised"
            >
              All releases on GitHub
              <span class="font-mono text-[11px] opacity-60">&rarr;</span>
            </a>
          </div>
          <p
            class="mt-4 font-mono text-[11.5px] uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-ink-faint"
          >
            windows 10 / 11 &middot; x64 &middot; {INSTALLER_SIGNED
              ? 'signed'
              : 'unsigned'} &middot; no telemetry
          </p>
        </section>
      </article>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
